    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass with a green build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule on `POST /api/owners`, read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The value is fixed at creation time (whether >80 owners had already been created today), so it's persisted on the owner like the other derived fields (`namesakeCount`, `customerCode`, etc.).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 set `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(createdToday > 80)`, reusing the existing `createdToday` count (owners sharing the new owner's registration date, excluding the not-yet-saved new owner). \"More than 80 already created today\" \u2192 `> 80`.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `bulk_signup_warning` column with a getter that coalesces null to `false` (so the response is always a concrete boolean, never null).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `bulkSignupWarning` as a read-only boolean on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it by name.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column to the hsqldb (used by tests), h2, mysql, and postgres schema files.\n\nThe new `Cp22Tests` (fresh create \u2192 `false`) passes, and the full suite is green (33/33), so nothing regressed.",
